    {
      "title": "Ready to share 'battle-tested' anti-terror expertise with Asean: Rajnath",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/ready-to-share-battle-tested-anti-terror-expertise-with-asean-rajnath-126102900470_1.html",
      "description": "India is ready to share its \"battle-tested\" counter-terror expertise with ASEAN and its dialogue partners, Defence Minister Rajnath Singh said on Thursday as he described Operation Sindoor as a declaration of New Delhi's clear approach against state-sponsored terrorist activities.\nThe defence minister also said that India supports an Indo-Pacific that is secure and resilient -- one where peace and stability are not merely aspirations, but the outcome of collective efforts.\nIn an address at a conclave of defence ministers of ASEAN member states and the bloc's dialogue partners in Cebu in the Philippines, he flagged concerns over disruptions in certain maritime trade routes and asserted that India will continue to act as a \"trusted net security provider\" in the Indian Ocean region and the wider Indo-Pacific.\n\"Today, when global trade routes are facing new types of international threats, merely issuing statements on maritime security is not enough,\" he said at the ASEAN Defence ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T06:51:12"
    }
